# Context

## Background
Commit 8a1dc88 appended hostile-pattern findings (Diagnostic[]) to the
inspect artifact. TypeScript interfaces get no implicit index signature,
so Diagnostic[] is not assignable to the Json recursive type. The
artifact failed typecheck at stableJsonStringify(artifact) while the
study-ir cascade was in flight, which masked the break.

## Why This Way
apps/cli/src/diagnostics.ts already had a private diagnosticToJson
serializer that emits the canonical diagnostic shape validated by
schemas/diagnostic.v1.schema.json. Exporting it keeps one serializer
instead of a hand-rolled mapping in the handler.

## Gotchas
- A Json-typed object literal cannot hold interface values like
  Diagnostic even when every field is Json-compatible. Route them
  through diagnosticToJson.
- Related: eb271d9, 413242b, d8a0630 embed only Json values, so they
  never hit this.
